  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable citrus chain empowering and developing smallholders in the Mekong Delta</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at making the citrus sector of the Mekong Delta more sustainable, more efficient, and more profitable for 2,250 citrus smallholders (750 smallholder farmers and 2 key staff members per farm).This goal will be achieved by developing a sustainable citrus value chain, in which farmers will be contracted and supported, through a private sector extension system, fertilizer advisory service, access to virus free citrus seedlings and access to a finance programme, in order to increase their incomes by least 50%.These interventions will reduce the negative impacts of agrochemicals on the environment and human health, as well as reduce the use of surface and ground water.</narrative>
  </description>
